    "title": "How Much Snow Did You Get? Check Latest Totals in Your Neighborhood",
    "text": "Janice Huff’s weather forecast for Friday, Jan. 5. Thursday's monster snowstorm is over, and it was a big one. National Weather Service numbers show that large swaths of the region saw more than a foot of snow from the powerful storm system; check the numbers in your neighborhood using the interactive map below. You can also click here for the latest numbers by neighborhood in New Jersey, where several counties had recorded more than a foot and a half by early afternoon, and here for the latest New York and Connecticut numbers. Note: The National Weather Service usually updates observed totals hourly, but timing may vary. MORE SNOW COVERAGE: Everything you need to know about the crippling nor'easterStorm Team 4 breaks down storm timeline, what to expectYour guide to mass transit, roads and air travelTrack the storm using interactive radar; School closings What to Expect: Storm Team 4 Breaks Down Latest Snow Projections, Timeline 1 of 14 DailyFindsDigest | The plumber's secret: how to unclog your drain with 1 simple ingredientUndoConsumer Reviews | We've tested 27 popular teeth whitening products: Here are the 5 winnersUndoOnline Shopping Tools | Amazon Nightmare Comes True: Shoppers Canceling Prime For This Clever HackUndohear.com | Americans Over 60 Are Ditching Hearing Aids for This New DeviceUndo",
